Below is a formal, engine-ready value formula system that defines how weapons, armor, gear, items, buffs, and effects are numerically valued for PvE and PvP separately.
This is the kind of math used internally by AAA MMOs to keep balance stable.

I’ll structure this as canonical formulas + rules + caps, so you can drop this directly into UE5 (Blueprint/C++), spreadsheets, or server logic.

1️⃣ Core Principle (Very Important)
Item Value ≠ Item Level ≠ Power

We separate four layers:

Raw Stat Value (numbers on item)
Effective Power (combat math)
Context Multiplier (PvE vs PvP)
Encounter Modifier (boss, arena, scaling)
2️⃣ Base Stat Value Formula (Universal)
Every stat is converted into Power Units (PU).

StatValuePU = RawStat × StatWeight × ScalingCurve
Example Stat Weights (baseline)
Stat	Weight
STR / DEX / INT	1.00
VIT / CON	0.85
Crit Chance	2.50
Crit Damage	1.75
Attack Speed	2.00
CDR	2.25
Armor	0.75
Resistance	0.90
PvP Resilience	3.00
These weights differ slightly for PvE and PvP (see section 7).

3️⃣ Scaling Curves (Anti-Overflow Protection)
Linear (early game)
ScalingCurve = 1.0
Soft Cap Curve (recommended)
EffectiveStat = RawStat / (RawStat + SoftCap)
ScalingCurve = EffectiveStat × SoftCap
Diminishing Returns (PvP, CC, Crit)
EffectiveValue = Cap × (1 - e^(-RawStat / K))
4️⃣ Weapon Power Formula
4.1 PvE Weapon Power
WeaponPower_PvE =
(
  BaseDamage × WeaponSpeedFactor
+ AttributeScaling
+ ElementalScaling
)
× PvEMultiplier
Where:

AttributeScaling = (MainStat × StatCoef)
ElementalScaling = Σ(ElementDamage × ElementCoef)
Example
PvEWeaponPower =
(1200 × 1.1 + (STR × 2.5) + (Fire × 1.3)) × 1.0
4.2 PvP Weapon Power (Normalized)
WeaponPower_PvP =
(
  NormalizedBaseDamage
+ AttributeScaling × PvPStatScale
)
× PvPDampening
Typical values:

PvPStatScale = 0.65
PvPDampening = 0.75–0.85
This prevents burst one-shots.

5️⃣ Armor & Defense Value Formula
5.1 Armor Mitigation
DamageMitigation =
Armor / (Armor + K × AttackerLevel)
Where:

K = 50–100 (tuning constant)
5.2 Total Defensive Power (TDP)
TDP =
(
  HP × HPWeight
+ Armor × ArmorWeight
+ Resistance × ResistWeight
)
× SurvivalMultiplier
Example:

TDP = (HP×0.4 + Armor×0.3 + Resist×0.3) × 1.0
6️⃣ Gear Score / Item Power Formula
This is what UI usually shows.

ItemPower =
Σ(StatValuePU)
+ ProcValue
+ SetBonusValue
Proc Valuation
ProcValue =
(EffectMagnitude × Uptime × ImpactWeight)
Example:

BurnProcValue = (300 DPS × 0.25 uptime × 1.2) = 90 PU
